{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Journey to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – The Arrival in the Fair City of Tokyo**\n\nFirst to the bustling streets of Edo’s heir where neon lights do dance and skyscrapers pierce the heavens. Here thou shalt spend three nights in the grand abodes of the Ginza or the serene gardens of Asakusa. Visit the hallowed halls of the Meiji Shrine where whispers of the ancestors may be heard. In the evening feast upon sushi fresh as morning dew or tempura crisp as autumn’s first leaf. Let not the Kabuki-za’s stage pass thee by for it is a sight to stir the soul.\n\n**Act I: Scene II – The Pilgrimage to the Ancient Capital of Nara**\n\nFrom Tokyo’s frenzy take the swift Shinkansen eastward to Nara the storied where deer do roam as tamely as court jesters. Spend a day among the towering Buddha at Todai-ji and the sacred kami at Kasuga Taisha. Let the gentle beasts nuzzle thy palm for they are messengers of the gods. Dwell in a ryokan where the tatami mats are soft as a lover’s sigh and the onsen waters warm thee to thy core.\n\n**Act II: Scene I – The Imperial City of Kyoto**\n\nNow to Kyoto the thousand-year-old where emperors once walked and geisha still glide like swans upon the pond. Spend five nights in this city of temples and teahouses. First to Kinkaku-ji where the golden pavilion gleams as though plucked from heaven’s own breast. Then to Fushimi Inari’s vermilion gates that scale the mountain like a ladder to paradise. In the Arashiyama bamboo grove let the whispering leaves sing thee lullabies. And when the sun dips low seek out the Gion’s lantern-lit alleys where maiko dance and the past lingers like perfume.\n\n**Act II: Scene II – The Enchanting Isle of Miyajima**\n\nFrom Kyoto’s embrace travel to Hiroshima’s gate and then by ferry to Miyajima’s sacred isle. Here the torii gate of Itsukushima stands as though it floats upon the tide a vision of the divine. Walk the island’s paths and let the deer and monkeys share thy path. Spend a night in a ryokan where the sound of waves shall lull thee to sleep.\n\n**Act III: Scene I – The Northern Enclave of Kanazawa**\n\nTake the Hokuriku Shinkansen northward to Kanazawa where samurai once drew their swords in the name of the Maeda clan. Wander the Kenrokuen gardens where every stone and stream is placed with purpose. In the Higashi Chaya District let the geisha’s laughter dance upon the evening air. Dwell in a machiya townhouse where the scent of matcha tea and ink do linger.\n\n**Act III: Scene II – The Frozen Wastes of Hokkaido**\n\nFrom Kanazawa’s gentler climes take flight to Hokkaido’s wild and untamed shore. In Sapporo the capital let the snow festival’s ice sculptures awe thee and the miso ramen warm thy bones. Venture to the Daisetsuzan’s peaks where hot springs bubble forth and the wild bears roam. Spend a night in a glass igloo where the stars shall be thy canopy and the Northern Lights thy curtain call.\n\n**Epilogue: The Farewell**\n\nWhen thy time in Nippon’s embrace draws nigh return to Tokyo’s embrace. In the final hours let the Shibuya Crossing’s chaos charm thee and the last of thy yen be spent upon a trinket to remember thy journey by. Then to Narita or Haneda’s gates where thou shalt board the plane and leave behind but carry ever in thy heart the memories of a land where old and new in perfect harmony reside.\n\n**Thus concludes this most wondrous itinerary devised for thy voyage to the Land of the Rising Sun.**", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.35541605949401855}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.04432947561144829}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.4927285313606262}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.5302392840385437}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -4.529942543740617e-06}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -4.291525328881107e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.18280933797359467}, {"token": "i